  "splashSummary": "A complete toolkit for phylogenomics: fetch GenBank records or organize FASTA loci, align, test saturation, concatenate and build trees.",
  "splashStart": "Start App",
  "splashStep1": "Load genomes or individual markers (COI, 12S, CYTB…) from NCBI, or local GenBank and FASTA files. [[SynGenes]] builds the marker searches from every synonym of each gene and standardizes the marker names for the next steps.",
  "splashStep2": "Inspect imported records, refine species names and recover taxonomy from GBIF, NCBI or SALVE with [[dataFishing]] before marker selection.",
  "splashStep3": "Choose which feature types (CDS, rRNA, tRNA) enter the analysis, or show SPLACE where FASTA headers keep the sample and locus names.",
  "splashStep4": "Pick the markers for the matrix and review missing and duplicated sequences in the gene presence and length heatmaps.",
  "splashStep5": "Align each marker with [[MAFFT]] and trim it with [[trimAl]] or [[ClipKIT]], keeping whole codons in protein-coding loci.",
  "splashStep6": "Test substitution saturation by codon position with the index of [[Iss (saturation)|Xia]] and decide which positions to keep.",
  "splashStep7": "Concatenate the aligned loci into a supermatrix and export NEXUS, PHYLIP and partition files, optionally split by codon position.",
  "splashStep8": "Estimate the maximum-likelihood phylogeny with [[IQ-TREE 3|IQ-TREE]] or [[RAxML-NG]], with branch support and optional per-gene trees.",
